course: dictionary
lesson: 1517
title: The word cent
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cent is a small coin or amount of money. A hundred cents make one dollar or one euro. When you see «N cents», the word tells you how much money it is, just like «N pounds» or «N apples».
explain: «Mia pays 1 dollar for 2 apples that cost 45 cents each.» The apples cost 90 cents altogether, so the change is 100 - 90 = 10 cents. You can count in cents the same way you count any small things.
explain: «Per cent» is a different phrase with the same root. It means out of a hundred, so «50 per cent» means half. Look at the words around cent to tell which meaning you have: money, or out of a hundred.
fact: A cent is a small amount of money.
fact: 100 cents make 1 dollar or 1 euro.
fact: The sign for cents is ¢, so 45¢ means 45 cents.
fact: «Per cent» means out of a hundred: 50 per cent is half.
fact: In the UK, coins are called pence and pound, but Australia, Canada, New Zealand and Ireland use cents.
exercise: «Mia pays 1 dollar for 2 apples that cost 45 cents each.» How many cents come back as change? | 55 cents | *10 cents | 45 cents | 90 cents
exercise: «Eggs cost 25 cents each.» How many cents do 12 loose eggs cost? | 250 cents | 120 cents | 37 cents | *300 cents
exercise: «Half of the class chose red, which is 50 per cent.» What does per cent mean here? | Per cent means a small coin | Per cent means one dollar | Per cent means very quick | *Per cent means out of a hundred
test: How many cents make 1 dollar? | 1000 | 50 | *100 | 10
test: «Found a tiny coin with no owner to ask.» Is that the same meaning as «a cent»? Choose the best answer. | No, it means very old | No, it is a sign for a dollar | *Yes, cent is money, so this is a small amount of money | No, it means out of a hundred
exam: «A dozen eggs cost 300 cents loose, but a box of 12 costs $2.50.» How many cents does the box save? | 250 cents | 300 cents | 25 cents | *50 cents
